==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*4 [[Le'boin]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 60~66.67 seconds<sup>1,800f~2,000f</sup>.
*20 [[Hippoe]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 6~20 seconds<sup>180f~600f</sup>.
*12 [[Jackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 0.67~4 seconds<sup>20f~120f</sup>.
*12 [[Zackie Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 0.67~4 seconds<sup>20f~120f</sup>.
*12 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 0.67~4 seconds<sup>20f~120f</sup>.
*1 [[Spacefish Jones]] spawns after 60 seconds<sup>1,800f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use plenty of meatshields to keep the Star Pengs at bay along with something to manage the Zackie Pengs like [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], [[Li'l Bird Cat (Special Cat)|Li'l Flying Cat]], [[Brainwashed Fish Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Fish Cat]], and/or [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]]. The Star Pengs are still extremely buffed even with all treasures, so a [[:Category:Nuker-class Cats|Nuker]] like [[Catman (Uber Rare Cat)|Catman]] or [[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]] will be extremely helpful, along with a [[Talents|Talented]] [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]] or [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]. After all the Star Pengs and Zackie Pengs have been defeated, deal with the Le'boins and Spacefish Jones with [[:Category:Rusher-class Cats|Rushers]] or long-ranged units.

==Trivia==
*The Japanese name of this stage, Kichinto Kitchin (きちんとキッチン, "Tidy Kitchen"), may be a reference to the chicken brand Kichinto Chikin (きちんとチキン, "Neat Chicken")

